setup /usr/local/cuda -> /usr/local/cuda-9.2

and cd /usr/bin
sudo cp -sf /usr/local/cuda/bin/* .

That's for the PATH! You can always change /usr/local/cuda to point to the correct cuda version w/o having to change anything else


----
Thereafter go and change this

cat /etc/ld.so.conf.d/cuda.conf 
/usr/local/cuda/lib64/

Run sudo ldconfig

That's it!! It will no how to find your .so files correctly everafter
